From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 17:28:51 -0500
Subject: fix: keep the names people gave their tabs in Arc

A tab renamed in Arc came in with that name as the title of a page not yet
loaded, or lost it to Arc's saved title, so the page's own title replaced it at
the first load, and for good. Arc keeps such a name in the item's title, which it
leaves null otherwise.

That name is now the tab's name, as a rename here makes one: written to the
session, and shown over the page's title. It holds for a pin, an essential, a tab
of a folder and a loose tab, through the first load and through a pin closing
back to its home. A sidebar file Stedding wrote leaves that field empty, so it
behaves as before.

No real Arc file was read: the field is as public exporters read it. A name Arc
kept only in savedTitle could not be told from a page's title.

Why: a person's own names are the first thing they see after an import, and they
went at the first click (BACKLOG S-431, GitHub issue 80, import I3).

Removable when: Arc's files are gone from people's computers.
